==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|la}} {{term|invidiosus|invidiōsus|lang=la}} < {{term|invidia||envy, ill will|lang=la}} < {{term|in-||upon|lang=la}} + {{term|video|videō|I see|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɪnˈvɪdiəs/}}
* {{audio|en-us-invidious.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|ɪdiəs}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# (of a distinction) [[offensive]]ly or [[unfair]]ly [[discriminate|discriminating]]
#: ''The professor made '''invidious''' distinctions based only on his own whim.''
# (of an action or task) causing ill will towards the actor; causing offense.
# (of a thing) causing envy or ill will towards the possessor
# [[envious]], [[jealous]].
# (obsolete) [[hateful|Hateful]]; [[odious]]; [[detestable]].

